From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anxelok <anxelok@localhost>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 18:11:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tick in parallel unconditionally and remove the on/off flags

Parallel world, chunk, and entity ticking and the caller-participates
scheduling were each gated behind a -Dloom.* flag that defaulted on. There is
no reason to run any of them off, so drop the flags and the serial-fallback
branches they gated: the world loop always fans the levels out, chunk and
entity ticking always dispatch by region, the join always lets the dispatching
thread run buckets, and the block-state read relaxation always applies on a
tick thread. The region pool size and bucket granularity stay configurable;
only the redundant on/off toggles are gone.

