-    public static final boolean PARALLEL_WORLDS_ENABLED = !"false".equalsIgnoreCase(System.getProperty("loom.parallelWorlds"));
     // Loom - non-adjacency buffer (in chunks) between region-task buckets that run in parallel. A block
     // update fans out at most ~1 chunk, so buckets within this many chunks of each other are merged to tick
     // together, guaranteeing parallel buckets cannot race on a shared edge chunk. This is the load-bearing
     // safety primitive for intra-world parallel ticking. Higher = safer but coarser (less parallelism).
     static final int REGION_TASK_BUFFER_CHUNKS = Math.max(0, Integer.getInteger("loom.regionTaskBufferChunks", 1));
-    // Loom - intra-world parallel chunk ticking (Stage 3), ON by default. Disable with
-    // -Dloom.parallelChunkTick=false. When enabled, the per-chunk tick (random ticks + chunk block updates) is
-    // dispatched as region-bound tasks and non-adjacent regions tick concurrently on the region pool. This is
-    // the first wired tick phase of intra-world regions.
-    public static final boolean PARALLEL_CHUNK_TICK_ENABLED = !"false".equalsIgnoreCase(System.getProperty("loom.parallelChunkTick"));
-    // Loom - intra-world parallel entity ticking, ON by default. Disable with -Dloom.parallelEntityTick=false.
-    public static final boolean PARALLEL_ENTITY_TICK_ENABLED = !"false".equalsIgnoreCase(System.getProperty("loom.parallelEntityTick"));
-    // Loom - true when ANY parallel tick phase is enabled. Used as a cheap gate for owner-domain read
-    // relaxations: when this is false the server ticks fully serially and owner-aware read fast-paths must be
-    // skipped so the serial/default code path stays byte-identical.
-    public static final boolean PARALLEL_ANY_ENABLED = PARALLEL_WORLDS_ENABLED || PARALLEL_CHUNK_TICK_ENABLED || PARALLEL_ENTITY_TICK_ENABLED;
-    // Loom - caller-participates scheduling, ON by default. Disable with
-    // -Dloom.scheduler.callerParticipates=false. The intra-tick dispatch is a nested fork-join: the
-    // server thread fans the worlds onto the region pool, and each world-tick thread then fans its
-    // own chunk/entity buckets onto the SAME pool and waits at join(). A thread parked at join is a
-    // worker slot lost - it holds a pool thread while doing nothing. With this on, the dispatching
-    // thread does not park: it pulls ready buckets from a shared cursor and runs them itself,
-    // becoming one more in-window worker, and only waits for buckets still being run by other
-    // threads. Each bucket still runs exactly once under its own region context/lease, the per-world
-    // apply stays serial, and the phase ordering (chunk -> block events -> entity) is unchanged. Only
-    // the scheduling of the compute differs, so the commit model and plugin-visible behaviour are
-    // identical to the parked-join path.
-    public static final boolean CALLER_PARTICIPATES = !"false".equalsIgnoreCase(System.getProperty("loom.scheduler.callerParticipates"));
